EXT. ROADSIDE, STALLED SCHOOL BUS - AFTERNOON

Heat shimmer. Corn on both sides. The hood is up and smoke curls from the engine.

MR. EZRA PLUMLEY (50s, driver, cap pulled low) peers at the radiator. On the curb, four teens sit in a row. TOBIAS KRALL (16, lanky, headphones). NGOZI ADEBAYO (16, braids, a worn paperback). RAFFERTY "RAFF" BOONE (17, football jacket, bouncing knee). MEI-LIN SOONG (15, sketchbook shut).

RAFF
How long?

PLUMLEY
Until it stops smoking.

RAFF
That's not a time.

NGOZI turns a page. Doesn't read it.

TOBIAS pulls one earphone out. Puts it back.

MEI-LIN
Raff, you're shaking the curb.

RAFF
I'm not.

He is. He stops. Starts again.

PLUMLEY
Somebody toss me the water jug.

Nobody moves. Tobias stands. Gets the jug from the bus steps. Hands it over without a word. Sits again, closer to Ngozi than before.

NGOZI
(not looking up)
You hate this book.

TOBIAS
I never said that.

NGOZI
You've been holding it upside down for ten minutes.

He looks. She's right. He turns it. She hides a smile in the page.

RAFF
Okay, seriously. We're missing the game.

MEI-LIN
It's a scrimmage.

RAFF
It's the scrimmage.

PLUMLEY
(from under the hood)
Not today, son.

Raff kicks a pebble into the corn. Silence. Plumley's wrench clinks. A crow somewhere.

MEI-LIN
Raff.

RAFF
What.

MEI-LIN
Your dad's not coming, is he.

Raff stops. His whole body stops. The knee, the hands, the breath.

NGOZI closes her book. TOBIAS takes off his headphones, finally.

RAFF
I told him two-thirty.

MEI-LIN
It's four.

RAFF
He's probably stuck behind a tractor.

Nobody answers. Plumley slams the hood. The smoke is gone.

PLUMLEY
All right, folks. Load up.

They rise in order. Raff last. He looks down the empty road one more time, then climbs the steps and sits alone, three seats from anyone, jacket collar up.
